    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0280" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/581.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 14. The rebellion not anti foreign. Rebels as well as loyalists
                    disposed to protect foreigners. Except from Hankow and vicinity there seems to
                    be no need for removal of Americans. Steady movement of troops southward.
                    Russians have ordered troops to Suppress Hunghutzus in Manchuria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
